   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "What didn't happen",
     "texto": [
      "For an imaginary situation in the past, use **hvis** + an auxiliary in the past (**havde** or **var**) + participle in the condition, and **ville** + the corresponding auxiliary + participle in the result.",
      "Example: **Hvis jeg havde haft tid, ville jeg være kommet.** = If I had had time, I would have come. **Komme** forms the perfect with **være**.",
      "With other verbs **have** is used: **Hvis jeg havde været der, ville jeg have set det.** = If I had been there, I would have seen it."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Without «ville»",
     "texto": [
      "In the main clause you can also use just **havde** + participle: **Hvis du havde ringet, havde jeg hjulpet dig.** = If you had called me, I would have helped you.",
      "It's just as correct and very normal when speaking."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
